From: NeoDarwin
Subject: [PATCH] zfs_file_getattr(): the file type comes from the vnode

vdev_file_open() refuses a file vdev whose zfs_file_getattr() mode isn't
S_ISREG(). The macOS layer returns the vnode's va_mode, whose type bits
depend on the file system: HFS+ sets them, ZFS's own getattr
(zfs_vnops_os.c, va_mode = z_mode & ~S_IFMT) clears them. So a pool on
files kept in a ZFS dataset, as many OpenZFS tests make one (zpool_create,
zpool_status, zpool_import: files under TESTDIR or /testpool), failed with
ENODEV, "no such device in pool" (P3-01 checkpoint 2). The type now comes
from vnode_vtype(), as FreeBSD's VOP_GETATTR() and Linux's vfs_getattr()
give it.

Rebase-risk: low
---
diff --git a/module/os/neodarwin/zfs/zfs_file_os.c b/module/os/neodarwin/zfs/zfs_file_os.c
--- a/module/os/neodarwin/zfs/zfs_file_os.c
+++ b/module/os/neodarwin/zfs/zfs_file_os.c
@@ -342,6 +342,25 @@
 
 	zfattr->zfa_size = vap.va_size;
 	zfattr->zfa_mode = vap.va_mode;
+#ifdef __NEODARWIN__
+	/*
+	 * va_mode's file type bits are the file system's to give: HFS+
+	 * includes them, ZFS's own getattr (zfs_getattr()) leaves them
+	 * out. Take the type from the vnode, so a file vdev on a ZFS
+	 * dataset passes vdev_file_open()'s S_ISREG() check.
+	 */
+	zfattr->zfa_mode &= ~S_IFMT;
+	switch (vnode_vtype(filp->f_vnode)) {
+	case VREG: zfattr->zfa_mode |= S_IFREG; break;
+	case VDIR: zfattr->zfa_mode |= S_IFDIR; break;
+	case VBLK: zfattr->zfa_mode |= S_IFBLK; break;
+	case VCHR: zfattr->zfa_mode |= S_IFCHR; break;
+	case VLNK: zfattr->zfa_mode |= S_IFLNK; break;
+	case VSOCK: zfattr->zfa_mode |= S_IFSOCK; break;
+	case VFIFO: zfattr->zfa_mode |= S_IFIFO; break;
+	default: break;
+	}
+#endif
 
 	return (0);
 }
